<<~ aka lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/RFC-2119#normative-language >>

<<^ &#x0002; >>

<<~ ahu #head >>

! The Guild of Lamplighters

''A herm stands where nobody watches.'' It carries, it serves the public shelf, it holds every sovereign act closed — and canon gives it no tender at all: a lost or soured Herm ''re-establishes from its operator'' (`identity-classes#herm-establishment`). That leaves two holes the mesh feels before it feels anything else.

''The first hole reads ABANDONMENT.'' An operator who walks away strands a crossroads, because re-establishment runs through that one hand.

''The second reads GRAY FAILURE, and it costs more.'' `waking-floor#the-open-question` prices it: a power-cutter holds a ''permanent deniable veto'' — silent capability suppression rather than a legible outage — and peers ''cannot distinguish a vessel at the floor from one compromised and imitating it''. A lone herm cannot surface its own suppression.

''The Guild answers both with many hands and no owner.'' Lamplighters patrol, notice, and repair. They hold no read-cap, no persona, and no verdict.

!!! The myth carried it, warning included

Rome's ''collegia compitalicia'' tended the crossroads shrines, drawn from freedmen and slaves — and the Senate suppressed them, because a network of people who keep neighbourhood infrastructure alive holds real power. Athens learned the other half in 415 BC: the ''Mutilation of the Herms'' turned on the fact that herms stood everywhere ''unguarded'' — belonging to everyone, watched by no one. <<~ confidence Provisional-Synthesis 7/20 >> Both particulars ride memory rather than an opened source; the design reading survives either way, and the historical claim wants a citation before it hardens.

''So the Guild expects attack as infrastructure.'' Its resilience reads as ''nothing to seize'': no read-caps, no roster, no central register of who tends what.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #office >>

!! Kuleana ~ the OFFICE, and why not "residency"

''The word `residency` stands spoken for three times over'' — thermal stowage (`wela`/`anu`), tiddler residency across bags, and which bag a carrier's file lives in. A fourth sense guarantees misroute. ''Name it `OFFICE` (`kuleana`)'': right and burden arriving on one name, and the house already speaks it (`hookupu-the-flow`, `convergent-mesh`).

''An office attaches to the PLACE, never to the person.'' Rome's ''vicomagistri'' held a college seat at a ''compitum''; the office belonged to the vicus, the person rotated through, and the shrine kept standing. <<~ confidence Synthesis 10/20 >>

\procedure ~Office(~Type:"" ~Params:"") ~Office <<~Type>> <<~holds `[<~Params>]`>>

<<~Office Grant "what/a-quorum-countersigns subject/the-vessel's-PLACE-DID requires/the-vessel's-own-contractSig ~ bilateral; a Nexus conscripts nobody" >>
<<~Office Fence "what/boundEpoch >= effectiveLeaseEpoch scope/per-Nexus ~ the same comparison device-delegation already makes" >>
<<~Office Ending "how/non-renewal ~ nobody exercises a lowering act; a newer grant binds higher and the frontier rolls past the old" >>
<<~Office Exception "when/a-malicious-self-renew rides/convergent-removal + kapae ~ never the counter" >>

!!! ★ THE QUORUM SEATS; THE QUORUM MUST NOT RENEW ★

''`attestation-plane` already rules the shape, and the naive transposition dies on it'':

> ''a quorum gates the rare, slow, high-power act, and automation carries the frequent, fast, low-power one. A quorum placed in the renewal path gets bypassed inside one outage, and the bypass becomes permanent.''

So the quorum ''seats'' an office (rare) and the ''renewal rides the lease-epoch roll'' (frequent), which any writer advances in its own per-writer slot. Rome ran it the same way: the election seats the magistri; tending the compitum daily needs no college.

!!! And the office reaches NO archive

`waking-floor#the-raise-is-a-vessel-layer-act` holds: a quorum's acts sit at ③ and reach ''no vessel's archive'', because a kahu holding shares becomes the collector. An office grant therefore opens nothing by itself.

''The ① answer that survives: an OFFICE KEY, never a persona key.'' A civic vessel mints a Place-DID-rooted office key at establishment; its archive holds that and no human's root. Opening it rides the raise door already standing — the vessel emits a nonce bound to its own epoch head, ''any current office-holder'' signs that, nothing touches disk. A human, yes; ''never THE operator''. That difference carries the whole vicomagistri property. <<~ confidence Synthesis 12/20 >>

''What it forfeits — unattended sovereign acts — a civic vessel mostly does not need.'' The civic FLOOR runs far larger than a hearth's: relay, public shelf, bulb, map-publish and segment-repair all stand with ''zero secret''. A district's service survives the power cut; only signing waits for a holder.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #immune >>

!! The immune coupling ~ innate, adaptive, memory

\procedure ~Layer(~Type:"" ~Params:"") ~Layer <<~Type>> <<~holds `[<~Params>]`>>

<<~Layer Innate "organ/lamplighters acts/patrol · notice · repair holds/tend caps ONLY ~ presents, never condemns" >>
<<~Layer Adaptive "organ/kahu-quorum acts/seat-a-presented-candidate holds/quorum-signature ~ the only condemning body" >>
<<~Layer Memory "organ/the-antigen shape/durable · convergent · per-Nexus ~ the emergency brake, never the default death" >>

!!! ★ PRESENTATION ⊥ CONDEMNATION ★

''A tender that could write the antigen turns the mesh against its own healthy nodes.'' The Guild runs as the most distributed and least-vetted body in the model — so it reads as the likeliest thing to get captured, and it therefore holds the ''sensor'' and never the ''verdict''. An autoimmune mesh costs more than a slow one.

!!! The antigen stays the emergency brake

RFC 2693 §7 rules the ordinary ending: //"under SPKI one does not declare a key to be bad but rather stops empowering it and instead empowers some other key"//. So ''non-renewal'' carries every ordinary death. The antigen answers the ONE case non-renewal cannot: a party ''actively renewing itself'' faster than waiting-out can reach.

!!! Herms present

''A herm stands a minimal `@daemon` carrying the Voice and a `@meshpalace` network vector store'' (operator ruling). So it holds a signing key, a publish surface on its own bearing, and a vector memory of its own network experience — and the ''victim testifies''. Gray failure gains its best sensor, because a herm being suppressed or probed reads as the one party that always knows.

''Presentations therefore carry a PROVENANCE-KIND.'' A tender saw from outside, a herm from inside; the two carry different capture profiles, and a quorum reads which arrived even at equal weight.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #zero-weight >>

!! ★ PRESENTATION CARRIES ZERO THRESHOLD WEIGHT ★

''The quorum needs its full k, always.'' N tenders converging lowers nothing.

!!! What the field does

''Nothing that carries durable, convergent consequence weights reports into a threshold.'' <<~ confidence Synthesis-Canon 15/20 >>

* ''Tor bad-relays'' — anyone reports; a fixed ''majority'' of directory authorities decides, whatever the volume.
* ''Ethereum slashing'' — any whistleblower presents; the protocol acts on ''cryptographic evidence'' (two conflicting signatures). One valid proof suffices; a hundred reports never do.
* ''Certificate Transparency'' — misbehaviour rides a ''consistency-proof failure'', a self-verifying artifact.
* ''TUF'' — thresholds stay static by design.
* ''PeerReview'' — evidence by log replay, ''irrefutable''; a correct node can always defend against false accusation.

''The one domain that DOES weight reads content moderation'' — and it ships ''report-brigading'' as its standing pathology. It survives there because a takedown ''reverses cheaply''. An antigen reverses at quorum cost, so the analogy does not transfer.

''Reputation-weighting collapses under Sybil pressure, measured rather than theorized'': EigenTrust falls to feedback-cliques, and the collaborative-IDS literature names the same shape ''poisoning''. <<~ confidence Canon 17/20 >>

!!! ★ And the structural argument closes it independent of security ★

''Counting N distinct presenters needs a tender set, and a tender set reads as a ROSTER.'' "Three tenders agreed" presupposes an agreed set at an agreed moment — a roster ''and'' a global now, both forbidden. Weighting does not merely risk capture here: ''it holds no well-defined N in this substrate''. Any implementation smuggles a roster back in.

!!! What recovers the speed instead

# ''Move the burden from COUNT to CONTENT.'' A presentation SHOULD carry a self-verifying artifact wherever the fault admits one — a signed contradiction, a lease-epoch violation, a replayable log excerpt. ''The report reads as TRANSPORT; the artifact reads as evidence.'' The quorum's k stays fixed because it now verifies rather than believes.
# ''Corroboration MAY steer ATTENTION, never the threshold.'' Which candidate a quorum reads first — priority ⊥ verdict.
# ''A necessary-presentation gate hands a captured guild BLOCKING power.'' If presentation ever becomes required, the quorum MUST retain the ability to self-present and condemn with no tender at all. Otherwise the design trades autoimmunity for ''immunodeficiency''.

!!! The counter-argument, stated fairly

//A fixed k gives the emergency brake a fixed latency — the quorum's assembly time — and an adversary who measures it operates inside it. Under a fast-moving compromise, N independent tenders converging carries real Bayesian evidence, and refusing to spend it refuses information the mesh paid to collect.//

''The refusal holds because the discount's value scales with tender INDEPENDENCE'' — exactly the quantity a capture destroys and a roster-free substrate cannot measure. The mesh would pay with leverage an adversary can acquire, for a speed-up it cannot verify it received.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #reach >>

!! The tending caps ~ split by REACH, never by body-location

''No design binds a cap to //a human body stood at the box//.'' <<~ confidence Synthesis-Canon 16/20 >> SPIFFE proves ''which node'', never where a hand acted; TPM quotes measure software state and carry no location; TCG physical-presence ships ''software'' methods of asserting the bit; FIDO user-presence proves ''someone touched'', never who. Anything claiming otherwise reads as theatre.

''So the split rides two caps named by REACH'':

<<~moves tend/island -> exercisable-over/a-path-with-no-remote-transport scope/this-herm >>
<<~moves tend/reach -> exercisable-over/the-network scope/this-herm >>

!!! Why the cap, and not the ceremony alone

# ''A ceremony leaves no artifact to non-renew.'' The default death runs by non-renewal, which needs a thing that expires. One cap with two admission rites yields one lease, and the remote half cannot be declined.
# ''The BMC record shows physical-adjacent planes silently becoming remote planes.'' IPMI, Redfish and the web console frequently share ''one user database''; a 2004-era authentication flaw still exposes hashes pre-authentication on tens of thousands of internet-reachable BMCs, and the field now calls IPMI a //sanctioned backdoor//. <<~ confidence Canon 17/20 >> One "tend" cap distinguished only by rite reproduces that collapse the first time anyone deploys out-of-band management.
# ''A cap persists as an auditable, presentable object'', where ceremony evidence dies at the moment performed.

''The ceremony still matters, riding ON TOP.'' It sets ''who may hold''; the cap sets ''what reach opens''. Both, in that order.

!!! ★ PHYSICAL TENDING READS AS DEATH AND REBIRTH, NEVER CONTINUITY ★

Physical access defeats confidentiality and forward integrity of a box outright — evil-maid on the unencrypted pre-boot path, DMA over Thunderbolt/PCIe, cold-boot key recovery from DRAM residue. <<~ confidence Canon 17/20 >>

''So a herm a hand touched emerges as a NEW identity'' — new key, new epoch — presented for re-admission through the ordinary path. This lands inside the house rather than against it: non-renewal stays the default death, and a re-admission needs no antigen.

''What the design still holds after a touch'':

* ''`carry ⊥ read`'' — a herm holds no read-cap, so a toucher harvests ciphertext. The correct physical-access defence, and it needs no hardware.
* ''Other islands'' — per-Nexus scope means a touched herm forges nothing about anyone else's history.
* ''The monotone lease epoch'' — non-renewal requires ''zero cooperation'' from the captured box.
* ''Evidence already published elsewhere'' — off-box tamper-evident logs stay probative.

''What the design MUST stop pretending to hold'':

* that a physical repair leaves prior key material uncompromised — treat every touched herm as ''key-disclosed'';
* that a post-touch attestation distinguishes a repaired herm from a re-imaged impostor — a toucher who reflashes the measurement root produces a well-formed quote of an attacker-chosen state;
* that physical presence implies authorization.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #open >>

!! ★ OPEN — the voice-capture question, unruled ★

''`tend.repair` scoped as admin over the herm's own island reaches that island's `@daemon` SIGNING KEY.'' A tender could then ''speak as the herm'' — and the innate layer could ''synthesize presentations that read as herm self-testimony'', which costs the mesh the independent sensor `#immune` just gained.

''The Guild would hold no read-cap over carried traffic and would hold the herm's VOICE.'' Two readings, and the operator has ruled neither:

* ''isolate'' the daemon signing key from the tending cap's blast radius; or
* ''accept'' it, name it, and price the loss of independent herm testimony.

<<~ confidence Provisional 4/20 >> The hazard itself wants checking before it wants ruling: no `tend.repair` cap stands in code yet, and the island-admin scoping came from a design sentence rather than from an implementation. The question to settle FIRST asks whether island-admin reads as the only shape that can re-key a soured leyline.

!!! Also owed

* ''The grammar half of belonging stands UNBUILT.'' A node belongs to a Nexus by ''contract'' AND by ''agreeing with the grammar vectors traded on it''; every grant this carrier designs rides the contract half alone, and //contract without grammar-agreement reads as a signature over an unread page//.
* ''Cross-Nexus gossip DEFERRED to post-founding'' (operator ruling). Keys run per-Nexus and no //act as a visitor// path stands, so a tender walking to another Nexus arrives carrying nothing and contracts in from zero.
* ''Nothing in the field welds place-anchored authority to term-bounded office.'' The nearest misses: CT's `previous_operators` (resolves the office-holder ''at the time of the act'', yet only to attribute), Kubernetes bound ServiceAccount tokens (term = the life of a place, no succession), DNSSEC root TCRs (real term-bounded office, ''procedural and legal, never cryptographic''), and SPKI §7.7 (held the whole vocabulary in 1999, shipped nothing).

<<~/ahu >>

